<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Personality</h1>
<p>When you create a character, you choose their personality, which sets 
where your alignment starts (see <a cmd='#'>Help Alignment</a>):
</p>
<pre>1) A saint               good, alignment +850
2) Who cares?            neutral, alignment 0
3) The devil's brother   evil, alignment -850
</pre>
<p>Your guild may limit the choice: healers and rangers can be good or 
neutral, paladins must be good, and necromancers and dark knights must be 
evil. Everyone else may choose freely.
</p><p>The choice matters: some guilds won't take players of the wrong 
alignment, and some spells work only for, or against, the good or the 
evil. Choosing good or neutral keeps you out of most trouble. It is only 
a start, though: your alignment changes with what you kill.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Alignment</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Guilds</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Login Guilds</a>
</pre>




</div>